<div data-anchor="study-associations" class="rug-read-more">
<div class="rug-read-more__container">
<div class="rug-read-more__content">
<a id="study-associations"></a>
<h2 class="">Study associations</h2>
<div class="">
<h3 class="rug-mt">Caerus</h3>
<div>
<div class="rug-theme--content rug-mb">
<div>Caerus is the study association of the University College
Groningen.</div>
</div>
<div class="rug-clearfix"></div>
</div>
<div>
<div class="rug-theme--content rug-mb">
<div>At the University College there are many diverse students with
different interest. In addition, all these students live together
at a campus. Caerus organizes many different activities to enhance
the community feeling and to broaden the horizons of the UCG
students.</div>
</div>
<div class="rug-clearfix"></div>
</div>
<a href="http://caerus-ucg.com/" target="_blank" xml:lang="en">http://caerus-ucg.com/</a>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<button aria-hidden="true" class="rug-read-more__toggle"><span class="rug-icon"></span><span class="rug-read-more__open-label">Read more</span><span class="rug-read-more__closed-label">Read less</span></button>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="rug-background-white rug-pv">
<div class="rug-wrapper">
<div class="rug-button--foldout js--id-foldout-container">
<a data-foldout-class="rug-button--foldout__active" data-id="foldout-N209B2" class="js--button-foldout rug-button--foldout__medium rug-button rug-button--neutral rug-button--medium js--analytics" data-hash-name="profile" name="profile" data-category="studentprofiel-extrainfo" data-action="bachelor" data-label="Liberal Arts and Sciences">Student profile<span class="rug-icon rug-pv-s rug-pl-xs rug-icon--user2"></span></a>
<div data-id="panel-N209B2" class="rug-panel rug-panel--foldout">
<div>
<div>
                  
<p>The world is changing rapidly, and the challenges we face are
increasingly complex. We are looking for students who are curious
about the world, eager to explore different perspectives and
connect them. You do not need to know what you want to do in the
future. What matters is that you are ready to take an active role
in your learning. Our students are ambitious and engaged. They want
to understand the world in all its complexity and develop the
knowledge and creativity to find their way in it.</p>
               
</div>
</div>
</div>
<a data-foldout-class="rug-button--foldout__active" data-id="foldout-N209C5" class="js--button-foldout rug-button--foldout__medium rug-button rug-button--neutral rug-button--medium js--analytics" data-hash-name="advice" name="advice" data-category="advies-extrainfo" data-action="bachelor" data-label="Liberal Arts and Sciences">(Binding) study advice<span class="rug-icon rug-pv-s rug-pl-xs  rug-icon--clipboard"></span></a>
<div data-id="panel-N209C5" class="rug-panel rug-panel--foldout">
<div>
<ul class="rug-list--bullets rug-mv-xs">
<li class="rug-list--bullets__item"> A minimum of 60  EC in the first 12 months  (binding)</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div>
<div>
                     
<p>Liberal Arts and Sciences at UCG is a demanding programme.
Students are expected to be highly motivated. Additionally, one of
the main characteristics of the programme is the emphasis on the
learning community. It is of importance that students as a class
stay together over the years. Students are expected to collect all
60 credits for the first year of the programme within the first
year.</p>
                  
</div>
</div>
</div>
<a data-foldout-class="rug-button--foldout__active" data-id="foldout-N209F0" class="js--button-foldout rug-button--foldout__medium rug-button rug-button--neutral rug-button--medium js--analytics" data-hash-name="support" name="support" data-category="support-extrainfo" data-action="bachelor" data-label="Liberal Arts and Sciences">Study support<span class="rug-icon rug-pv-s rug-pl-xs rug-icon--chat"></span></a>
<div data-id="panel-N209F0" class="rug-panel rug-panel--foldout">
<div>
<div>
                  
<p>At UCG, we encourage students to take ownership of their
education and shape their programme around their own interests and
ambitions. At the same time, you are never expected to navigate
your studies alone. Our dedicated guidance team, consisting of
Academic Advisors and Student Mentors, is there to support you
throughout your time at UCG.</p>
               
</div>
<div>
                  
<p>Your <strong>Academic Advisor</strong> helps you make informed
choices about your curriculum, from selecting courses and shaping
your Major and Minor to planning for future study and career
opportunities. Together, you can discuss your academic interests,
monitor your progress and identify potential challenges early on.
Your advisor can also help you consider how your course choices can
support your longer-term academic and professional goals.<br>
In addition, every first-year student is paired with a
<strong>Student Mentor</strong>. Student Mentors are fellow UCG
students who can help you settle into university life, find your
way around UCG and Groningen, and share their own experiences of
studying at UCG.<br>
Our guidance extends beyond academic planning. Academic Advisors
help students explore their options after UCG through career
advice, networking opportunities and events with alumni. This
personalised support gives you the space to develop as an
independent student while having guidance available whenever you
need it.</p>
               
</div>
</div>
</div>
